# focus_lost — the outcome, not the verb.
#
# A failed look that loses the thread: one noetic point beyond the three the look, the thinking and
# the attempt spent, and kept lost, because a failed act does not refill the pool at the CONTINUE
# that follows. Examine's whole table is this one entry; --penalty-only is passed anyway, so the
# script still means something the day the table grows. The pool is 6 (--organs encephalon=2): on a
# pool of 3 the attempt spends the last point and there is no thread left to lose.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Crown" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Giant Tree" --grant-mm woodcraft --means-only woodcraft --penalty-only lose_focus --organs encephalon=2

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy fail-dice
goal examine
advance 12 180

click observe "Test Giant Tree"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "Test Giant Tree"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180

# --- before: a pool of 6, of which the look and the thinking spent one each ---
expect-state noetic points=4/6

click act 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect FAILURE
expect-verb examine
expect Focus lost:

# --- the outcome really ran ---
expect-outcome focus_lost

# --- after: the attempt's point is gone, and the thread's with it ---
expect-state noetic points=2/6

# --- and stays gone across the result's CONTINUE ---
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-state noetic points=2/6
quit
